# An unterminated backtick raw string literal must be REFUSED, not silently
# swallowed to end of file. There is no escape for a backtick inside a raw
# literal, so the only terminator is the next backtick; when the file ends
# first, the scanner reports the OPENING line.
#
# tychoc rejects at the raw-literal scanner's terminator check
# (src/tychoc.c:536, "unterminated raw string literal"). Expected diagnostic:
#     tests/reject/rawstring_unterminated.ty:13: error: unterminated raw string literal
# The frozen tychoc0 has no backtick token at all, which is why no tychoc0 lane
# globs tests/reject/ (tests/run.sh:183).

fn main():
    s := `this literal never closes
    println(s)
